From 7e9c73d8b2d18784347571445f0b4a69d5ef7d19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/70] common/llama: cost-priced adaptive MTP draft depth
 (--spec-draft-adaptive, opt-in), per-width verify graphs

- MTP draft chain: with llama_set_mtp_draft_conf the chain graph also outputs the draft-head probability of each
  draft (softmax at the argmax) and the h_nextn of its last pass, so a chain continues in a next decode with the same
  drafts as one longer chain. The fixed-depth chain graph is unchanged.
- common_spec_depth_policy: drafts in segments of --spec-draft-seg levels (default 4) up to --spec-draft-n-max;
  c_k = prod q_j with q_j the acceptance of draft j given the earlier ones, learned live per draft-head probability
  bin and depth bucket (prior p^2, LLAMA_SPEC_DEPTH_POWER); kept depth maximizes sum c_j - R*v(k+1), one more
  segment while its extrapolated value exceeds R * segment ms. R = live tokens/ms of whole steps; v(w) timed at
  startup for every width (fastest of 7 decodes on empty memory), then the live per-width time and a live
  width-change cost.
- llama_set_verify_graph_cache: decodes of 2..N tokens that output every token keep a scheduler + graph per width
  [LLAMA_VERIFY_SCHED], enabled by the adaptive policy (LLAMA_VERIFY_SCHED=0 rebuilds). A width change otherwise
  costs ~1.6 ms per step (rebuild 1.24 ms + device graph update).

Server, Qwen UD, 6 prompts x 2 seeds, T=1, interleaved: n=4 mean 102.7/102.6 (chat 84.6, prose 93.5), n=5 103.0,
n=6 103.5, adaptive n-max 8 seg 4 103.6 (chat 79.8, prose 88.8), seg 2 102.4. Not a default: same mean as the best
fixed depth, chat/prose below n=4.
